  39:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_q31.c **** 
  40:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_q31.c **** /**
  41:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_q31.c ****  * @param[in] *pSrcA points to the first input sequence.
  42:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_q31.c ****  * @param[in] srcALen length of the first input sequence.
  43:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_q31.c ****  * @param[in] *pSrcB points to the second input sequence.
  44:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_q31.c ****  * @param[in] srcBLen length of the second input sequence.
  45:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_q31.c ****  * @param[out] *pDst points to the location where the output result is written.  Length srcALen+src
  46:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_q31.c ****  * @return none.
  47:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_q31.c ****  *
  48:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_q31.c ****  * @details
  49:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_q31.c ****  * <b>Scaling and Overflow Behavior:</b>
  50:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_q31.c ****  *
  51:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_q31.c ****  * \par
  52:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_q31.c ****  * This function is optimized for speed at the expense of fixed-point precision and overflow protec
  53:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_q31.c ****  * The result of each 1.31 x 1.31 multiplication is truncated to 2.30 format.
  54:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_q31.c ****  * These intermediate results are accumulated in a 32-bit register in 2.30 format.
  55:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_q31.c ****  * Finally, the accumulator is saturated and converted to a 1.31 result.
  56:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_q31.c ****  *
  57:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_q31.c ****  * \par
  58:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_q31.c ****  * The fast version has the same overflow behavior as the standard version but provides less precis
  59:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_q31.c ****  * In order to avoid overflows completely the input signals must be scaled down.
  60:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_q31.c ****  * Scale down the inputs by log2(min(srcALen, srcBLen)) (log2 is read as log to the base 2) times t
  61:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_q31.c ****  * as maximum of min(srcALen, srcBLen) number of additions are carried internally.
  62:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_q31.c ****  *
  63:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_q31.c ****  * \par
  64:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_q31.c ****  * See <code>arm_conv_q31()</code> for a slower implementation of this function which uses 64-bit a
  65:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_fast_q31.c ****  */
